# Line endings are LF in the repo AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true converts to CRLF on
# the way out, which puts the working tree at odds with Prettier's
# `endOfLine: "lf"` (.prettierrc.json): `npm run lint` then fails on every
# file in the repo, including ones nobody touched, and the only way to make it
# pass is to reformat the whole tree. `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf per
# repository, so the guard stays meaningful and contributors don't need
# matching global git config.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect and skip binaries; the repo currently
# tracks none, but the explicit rules below keep that true if any land.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
